==================================================================================
R12. CALIBRATION AND VALIDATION USE DISJOINT SEED BLOCKS
==================================================================================
  calibration seeds 900-919 (20 replications)
  validation  seeds 3000-3199 (200 replications)
  intersection: 0

  O'Brien-Fleming nominal levels: alpha1 0.0220, alpha2 0.0500
  calibrated:                     alpha1 0.0337, alpha2 0.0766  (common scale 1.532)
  achieved on the CALIBRATION set: 5.01%  (in-sample, reported for comparison only)

==================================================================================
R12. OVERALL TYPE I ERROR ON THE HELD-OUT VALIDATION SEEDS
==================================================================================
  Null cohort: every tau set to the margin, so this is the error rate at
  the boundary of H0. Intervals are 1.96 x Monte Carlo standard error.

  rule                                            error    MC SE   95% interval
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  zero-null, alpha 0.05 per look                  5.91%    0.05%   [5.82%, 6.01%]
  zero-null, calibrated                           4.98%    0.04%   [4.89%, 5.07%]
  matched-null, alpha 0.05 per look               3.86%    0.04%   [3.78%, 3.94%]
  matched-null, calibrated (primary)              4.98%    0.05%   [4.89%, 5.07%]

  The primary rule's interval is the one to read against the 5% target.

==================================================================================
R12. TYPE I ERROR UNDER DEPARTURES FROM THE REFERENCE MODEL
==================================================================================
  Same calibrated boundaries, held-out seeds, one departure at a time.
  The boundary uses the realized number of measurements in each arm. An
  earlier version used the nominal design count, which made the boundary
  too low whenever measurements went missing and pushed the error rate to
  6.16% at 10% missing and 7.57% at 20% missing.

  departure                                       error    MC SE   95% interval
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  reference (independent errors)                  4.98%    0.05%   [4.89%, 5.07%]
  within-period correlation, rho = 0.3            9.09%    0.07%   [8.96%, 9.23%]  <-- exceeds 5%
  within-period correlation, rho = 0.5           11.88%    0.07%   [11.75%, 12.02%]  <-- exceeds 5%
  10% of measurements missing                     4.91%    0.05%   [4.82%, 5.00%]
  20% of measurements missing                     4.88%    0.05%   [4.78%, 4.98%]
  20% dropout                                     5.06%    0.06%   [4.94%, 5.17%]
  onset ramp, time constant 2 weeks               2.17%    0.03%   [2.11%, 2.24%]
  washout 4 weeks                                 4.98%    0.05%   [4.89%, 5.07%]

==================================================================================
R18. THE BOUNDARY IS CALIBRATED AT ONE CV AND APPLIED AT ALL OF THEM
==================================================================================
  The calibration above was run at CV 0.15. The resulting alpha1 and
  alpha2 are then used unchanged at every CV the paper reports, so the
  5% claim is a claim about CV 0.15 and needs checking elsewhere. The
  critical value itself scales with CV, but the ratio statistic is not
  exactly normal and its departure from normality grows with CV, so the
  achieved error does not stay fixed.

  Audit seeds 4000-4099, disjoint from both the calibration and the validation blocks.

    total CV    error    MC SE   95% interval
  --------------------------------------------------------
        0.10    5.35%    0.06%   [5.24%, 5.46%]  <-- above 5%
        0.15    4.95%    0.06%   [4.84%, 5.06%]
        0.22    4.48%    0.06%   [4.37%, 4.59%]  reachable range
        0.26    4.25%    0.06%   [4.14%, 4.35%]  reachable range
        0.30    4.00%    0.06%   [3.89%, 4.11%]  reachable range
        0.36    3.63%    0.05%   [3.53%, 3.74%]

  The boundary is conservative over the model-implied reachable range 0.22 to
  0.30 and mildly liberal below the calibration point: at CV 0.10 the interval
  lies above 5%. We report the excess rather than hide it. A single fixed
  boundary is kept for the main analysis because a candidate trial fixes its
  standardization package, and therefore its assumed CV, before it starts; the
  consequence is that such a trial must calibrate its own boundary by simulation
  at that prespecified CV rather than reuse the numbers here.

==================================================================================
R12. OPERATING CHARACTERISTICS WITH MONTE CARLO UNCERTAINTY
==================================================================================
  Reference cohort, held-out seeds, primary rule.

  sensitivity           82.00%  MC SE 0.06%  95% interval [81.88%, 82.13%]
  specificity           99.32%  MC SE 0.04%  95% interval [99.25%, 99.39%]
  Stage 2 entry         24.57%  MC SE 0.07%  95% interval [24.43%, 24.71%]

==================================================================================
R12. WHY THE CALIBRATED ALPHA2 EXCEEDS 0.05
==================================================================================
  Stage 1 nominal 0.0220 -> calibrated 0.0337
  Stage 2 nominal 0.0500 -> calibrated 0.0766

  Stage 1 critical value: 25.8%
  Stage 2 critical value: 20.1%

  alpha2 is not a per-test level applied to an unselected patient. Only the
  patients whose Stage 1 estimate fell between the null margin and the Stage 1
  critical value reach the second look; those above were already called
  responders and those below were already called non-responders. alpha2 is the
  conditional level applied to that selected middle group, and the quantity
  constrained to 5% is the error of the whole procedure, not either look. A
  conditional level above 0.05 is therefore expected rather than anomalous, and
  the number to compare against 5% is the validated overall rate above.

  Reproduce with: python3 validation/sequential_error_validation.py

