====================================================================================
R4. WHAT TOTAL CV IS REACHABLE, BY VARIANCE COMPONENT
====================================================================================
  cv_bio is split into a part that sampling standardization can remove
  (diet, time of day, fasting state) and an irreducible day-to-day part.
  Duplicate assay divides only the analytical variance.

  scenario                                                none    std.  std.+dup
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  optimistic: 2/3 of biological CV is standardizable     0.372   0.219     0.215
  intermediate: 1/2 standardizable                       0.373   0.264     0.261
  pessimistic: 1/3 standardizable                        0.372   0.302     0.299

  The duplicate assay column differs from the column to its left by at
  most 0.0041. Re-assaying the same specimen cannot deliver the
  0.25 -> 0.15 reduction the manuscript previously attributed to a
  package that included it. Reaching 0.15 requires the irreducible
  biological component alone to be below 0.15.

====================================================================================
R4. WHAT IRREDUCIBLE BIOLOGICAL CV WOULD 0.15 TOTAL REQUIRE?
====================================================================================
  cv_pre=0.04, cv_analytical=0.06, replicates=2: cv_bio must be <= 0.138
  cv_pre=0.08, cv_analytical=0.06, replicates=2: cv_bio must be <= 0.120
  cv_pre=0.08, cv_analytical=0.06, replicates=1: cv_bio must be <= 0.112
  Against a reported within-person biological CV of 0.359, that is a
  reduction of more than half, for which there is no CKD evidence.

