================================================================================================
R5. THE LEVERS ARE NOT INDEPENDENT
================================================================================================
  Starting point: no standardization, 2x3 design, CV 0.373, sensitivity 49.3%

  add sampling standardization, keep 2x3          sens  65.2% (+15.9 pp),  29.3 wk,  14.6 venip
  keep CV, go to 4 cycles                         sens  61.1% (+11.8 pp),  53.3 wk,  26.6 venip
  keep CV, 4 measurements per period              sens  55.8% ( +6.5 pp),  30.2 wk,  20.2 venip
  standardization AND 3 cycles                    sens  70.1% (+20.8 pp),  40.4 wk,  20.2 venip
  standardization AND 4 measurements per period   sens  70.3% (+20.9 pp),  28.6 wk,  19.1 venip

  Standardization alone: +15.9 pp. Doubling cycles alone: +11.8 pp.
  Both (standardization + one extra cycle): +20.8 pp, against +27.7 pp if the two gains added.
  The levers act on the same standard error, so their effects are
  sub-additive; treating them as independent double counts the benefit.

================================================================================================
R14. THE EFFICIENCY CONCLUSION UNDER ALL THREE VARIANCE SPLITS
================================================================================================
  For each split the 2x3 design with no standardization is the baseline.
  Burden is weeks, venipunctures, and a qualitative patient-effort score
  (0 none, 1 timed fasting draws and a dietary log, 2 as 1 plus repeat
  assay logistics). Patient effort is not commensurable with weeks and is
  reported separately rather than folded into one index.

