##############################################################################
# threshold_approximation_check.py
##############################################################################
====================================================================================
DECISION-THRESHOLD APPROXIMATION ACCURACY
====================================================================================
  Analytic DT6 = 14.25%   null patients per scenario = 400,000   seed = 20260727
  AR(1) within blocks of 3; 2 independent blocks per arm

  scenario                      empirical p95   diff (pp)  empirical alpha
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Gaussian, iid (reference)            13.32%       -0.93            3.84%
  Log-normal IS baseline               13.34%       -0.91            3.89%
  Heteroscedastic CV                   13.79%       -0.45            4.50%
  AR(1) rho = 0.3                      15.94%       +1.69            7.22%
  AR(1) rho = 0.5                      17.64%       +3.39            9.64%

  Largest absolute deviation: 3.39 percentage points
  The approximation holds within 1 pp under the distributional violations
  and is mildly conservative there (empirical alpha below the nominal 5%).
  It breaks only under within-period serial correlation, where the analytic
  threshold is too permissive and the empirical Type I error rises above 5%.
  That is the direct cause of the specificity loss in scenarios D and D'.

  ANALYTIC CROSS-CHECK (independent of the simulation)
     rho   SD inflation   DT6 x inflation
  ---------------------------------------
     0.0          1.000            14.25%
     0.3          1.208            17.21%
     0.5          1.354            19.29%

  The inflation factor is [BLOCK + 2*sum((BLOCK-k)*rho^k)] / BLOCK, which does
  not depend on the number of blocks. Serial correlation therefore multiplies
  every design's threshold by the same constant and leaves the comparison
  between the two design levers unchanged: CV still enters DT linearly and the
  measurement count still as 1/sqrt(n).

  design      CV   n    DT iid   DT rho=0.5
  -----------------------------------------
  2x3       0.25   6     23.7%        32.1%
  2x3       0.15   6     14.2%        19.3%
  4x3       0.25  12     16.8%        22.7%
  3x3       0.15   9     11.6%        15.7%

  DT(CV=0.15, n=6) / DT(CV=0.25, n=12) = 0.8485, identical at every rho.
